-- title:
--   Puncturing μ_q at p: cokernel with H⁰ dividing q
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $q$ a natural number, and work with abelian sheaves (valued in `Ab.{1}`) on the small fppf site `smallFppfTopology specInt` of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$, whose objects $U$ are schemes over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$ with flat, locally of finite presentation structure morphism. Let $L$ and $C$ be such sheaves, and let $iC$ be an isomorphism of presheaves between the underlying presheaf of $C$ and the presheaf obtained by restricting, along the functor sending $U$ to its underlying scheme $U.\mathrm{left}$, the underlying presheaf of [`FppfKummerSES.muPAbelianSheafLifted q`](def/AlgebraicGeometry_FppfKummerProp17.html#L608), i.e. of the kernel on the big fppf site of the endomorphism [`FppfKummerSES.gmPowSelf q`](def/AlgebraicGeometry_FppfKummerProp17.html#L410) — the universe-lift of the $q$-th power map on the multiplicative-group abelian sheaf. Let $f : L \to C$ be a morphism of sheaves such that (i) for every object $U$ the map on sections over $U$ is injective, and (ii) for every $U$ and every section $s$ of $C$ over $U$, $s$ lies in the image of the map on sections over $U$ if and only if there is $a \in \Gamma(U.\mathrm{left}, \top)$ with $a - 1$ in the ideal generated by $p$ and $a\,(u_s - 1) = 0$, where $u_s \in \Gamma(U.\mathrm{left}, \top)^\times$ is the unit attached by [`FppfKummerSES.gmLiftedSectionUnit`](def/AlgebraicGeometry_FppfKummerProp17.html#L395) to the image of $iC(s)$ under the kernel inclusion into the lifted multiplicative-group sheaf. Then there exist a sheaf $Q$, a morphism $g : C \to Q$ and a proof $w$ that $f$ followed by $g$ is zero, such that the short complex $0 \to L \xrightarrow{f} C \xrightarrow{g} Q \to 0$ is short exact and $\#\,H^0_{\mathrm{fppf}}(\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z, Q)$, computed as `Nat.card (fppfCohomology specInt Q 0)`, divides $q$. (For $q = 0$ the divisibility assertion is vacuous; for $q \neq 0$ it forces this cohomology group to be finite.)
--
--   Classically, $f$ realises $L$ as the extension by zero $j_!j^*\mu_q$ along $j : \operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z[1/p] \hookrightarrow \operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$ inside $\mu_q$, the characterisation of its sections being the condition that the corresponding unit become trivial near the fibre at $p$; the quotient $Q$ is then concentrated at $p$, and the assertion bounds the order of its global sections by $q$. It is used in the non-finite branch of the multiplicative-type layer dichotomy [`AlgebraicGeometry.nonempty_iso_or_natCard_algHom_eq_one_and_exists_shortExact_of_sectionsEquiv_convPow_of_ne_two`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.nonempty_iso_or_natCard_algHom_eq_one_and_exists_shortExact_of_sectionsEquiv_convPow_of_ne_two).
